@startbpmn BP06_MeasureGoalProgress
lang en

output L1 "01_detailed/BP06_MeasureGoalProgress.bpmn"
output L2 "02_detailed/BP06_MeasureGoalProgress.bpmn"

' Provenance (never in a drawn note, lint rule 5):
'   - the drawing does NOT dispatch on the measure's type: a numeric check-in carries a value and a
'     boolean one carries done or not done, which are two permutations of ONE operation and are
'     discovered at Design, not asserted here. Drawing the gateway was premature: BR-28, ADR-069,
'     SA 2026-10-11 ("yes, premature, leave that to detail design")
'   - every measure is typed numeric or boolean; there is no untyped measure: BR-28, QB-13
'   - a measure's type is amendable, and amending it leaves the check-ins already recorded as they
'     stand, each in the type it was recorded under: BR-28, SA 2026-10-10
'   - NOTHING records that the type changed. A measure has no change history: that an operation
'     happened is the operation log's business, every user operation is logged, and no drawing
'     models it (DRW-27). This retires the dated type-change entry of SA 2026-10-12 together with
'     the gateway that wrote it: BR-28, SA 2026-10-16 ("logging user operations is done for all
'     user operations, so modelling it doesn't make sense")
'   - one editor per entity serves adding a measure and changing one alike, and nothing separated
'     the two chains but the fields they stored, so they are ONE request: UX-04, SA 2026-10-11.
'     Call site BP06.04 (Amend a progress measure) is RETIRED, its id never reused
'   - the only thing a measure OWNS is its check-in history, which goes with it unasked, so neither
'     removing nor archiving it discloses or asks anything, and neither draws an impact read or
'     an approval: a project parented on it survives minus the link where it is removed and
'     keeps its parent where it is archived, a parentless project being legal in any case. This
'     is the shape a task's deletion already has
'     (BP11.08). Call sites BP06.06 (See what removing a measure takes) and BP06.10 (See what
'     archiving a measure takes) are RETIRED, their ids never reused: BR-12, BR-17, BR-96,
'     BR-115, POL-11, ADR-066, SA 2026-10-16 ("archiving leaf items like measures do not require
'     an approve decision")
'   - the check-in history is the MEASURE's, and reading it is this process's act: the v1 key-result
'     surface is preserved, where a measure keeps its own dated data points. The per-goal history
'     of earlier that day is WITHDRAWN by its author, and with it BP05's read: SA 2026-10-16 ("so
'     my ruling that measure check-ins are always part of goal check-ins was wrong. Revert that")
'   - a measure tracks a current value against a target, which is the whole point of it: numeric
'     carries a start value, a target, a unit and a direction, with the current value initialized
'     to the start and moved by each check-in; boolean carries done and not done, starting at not
'     done. v1 kept exactly that and no note; the optional note per check-in is what v2 adds:
'     BR-28, SA 2026-10-16, tmp/Bearing-v1 (KeyResult: startValue, currentValue, targetValue)
'   - a check-in is one dated data point with an optional note: section 3
'   - the history is append-only, so a second check-in on one date is a second data point: section 3, SA 2026-10-10
'   - the current value is the latest check-in, and the start value until there is one, so nothing
'     records it twice: BR-28, DRW-10
'   - an archived item is frozen, so an archived goal's measures take nothing at all: BR-05, SA 2026-10-10
'   - a measure is archivable ON ITS OWN, so that one which turns out not to say anything about its
'     goal is set aside instead of deleted: BR-23, SA 2026-10-16 ("measures must be archivable on
'     their own if I notice that a measure does not work to fulfil a goal"). It reaches nothing: an
'     archived measure still exists, so a project parented on it keeps its parent, and it comes
'     back only into a live goal: BR-25, BR-26, BR-112
'   - archiving the GOAL still takes its live measures and its check-in history along unasked,
'     which is BP05's act and not drawn here: BR-112
'   - the Goals view carries the goal's ACTIVE measures, so an archived one is reached only through
'     the archive (BP15) and is frozen there like any archived item: BR-05, BR-26, BP05.01
'   - the goals overview carries no measures, so this process reads its own: BP05.01, section 7
'   - unfinished input is a draft, forms included: the field drafts as it is filled in, and the
'     operation that keeps it is drawn ONCE, in BP19, not per editing process. Here it is a
'     bound rule on the step that fills the field: BR-121, SA 2026-10-11
'   - the measure the user checks in on is already in front of them, read with the goals in
'     BP05.01, so no step of this process opens one: BP05.01, SA 2026-10-16 ("'Open a progress
'     measure' is part of BP05's read, so drop it from BP06")
'   - the cadence of a check-in is the user's, out of band: section 1.2 step 5
'   - per-measure status is auto-inferred at check-out, not at check-in: BR-28, BR-29
'   - a goal's progress measures are its sub-items and have no page of their own: they are read
'     with the goals, in BP05, and this process acts on what the Goals view already carries.
'     Call site BP06.08 (Read a goal's progress measures) is RETIRED and its id never reused.
'     An archived goal's measures are not reachable here, because the Goals view carries the
'     active goals only; BR-05 is held by the write's own verification: BR-05, BR-28, BR-87,
'     BR-128, SA 2026-10-14, ADR-066
'   - a deletion that discloses nothing still commits on a confirmation, so the step that
'     commits it reads as the confirmation, exactly as a disclosed deletion's does: DRW-28,
'     BR-20
'   - a step never enumerates the fields a request stores: which fields the entity carries is
'     a Detail Design matter and is not known yet, so the step names the act and its subject
'     only: SA 2026-10-14
'   - the box carries the act's own word, not the generic edit: the user DEFINES a measure:
'     SA 2026-10-16
'   - the check-in reads NOTHING first: the measures and where each one stands arrive with the
'     goals (BP05.01), and a view is read whole, so no act reads it again. The check-in is a write
'     and nothing else - state the value, submit it: BR-28, DRW-14, SA 2026-10-16 ("the current
'     measures are already available ... there is absolutely no need to read them")
'   - the dated series is the one thing the Goals view does not carry, and looking at how a measure
'     has moved is therefore an act of its own (OpenItem), not a preamble to the check-in: whether
'     a check-in form also shows the trend is the UI's business: BB02, DRW-14, SA 2026-10-16
'   - THE ACTS DO NOT RETURN to a hub: each act is one path and ends on what the gesture did. That
'     the measures stay in front of the user and the next act is available is the work loop, which
'     holds for every surface in the product and is stated once in the path patterns (BB22) instead
'     of being redrawn as a return edge per act - six return edges here, every one of them crossing
'     the drawing. The hub box was a return target and nothing else, so it is a plain step now, and
'     the "nothing more" exit went with the loop it closed: a gateway answer that does nothing is
'     not an act: BR-118, BB22, DRW-09, DRW-24, SA 2026-10-17 ("the loops make the diagrams
'     complicated")
'   - the check-in is ONE act, drawn the way every composed write is drawn: the box the user fills
'     in and the box that commits it. What is typed - the value and the optional note - is a draft
'     until the submit, which is why BR-121 binds on the first and the request leaves from the
'     second. A gesture that carries its own value and composes nothing is one box instead (pause
'     or resume, an order, a drag): BR-121, UX-04, DRW-11, BB03, SA 2026-10-16
'   - NOTHING IS FETCHED HERE. Every record is loaded once, at start-up (BP01), so a step that only
'     went to the store is gone, and one that selects or qualifies what the act works on says so
'     instead of saying read. What a chain still asks the system for is what it COMPUTES, which is
'     business and stays out of the client. When data is read is a detail design decision:
'     BR-128, DRW-14, SA 2026-10-17 ("when we will read data is not a business concern, but a
'     detail design decision ... I rule that this will be done once at startup")
'     Call site BP06.01 (Read a measure's check-in history) is RETIRED with the fetch it was, its id
'     never reused: the check-ins are in play with the measure, so looking at how one has moved asks
'     the system for nothing: ADR-066, SA 2026-10-17
'
'   - SETTING A MEASURE ASIDE needs a way back to it: the archive is reached by an explicit act,
'     from the surface that owns the kind, exactly as BP04, BP05, BP11 and BP17 reach it. The
'     measure is listed under its goal, in the Goals archive, and reading it, unarchiving it and
'     destroying it are BP15's - one step, a note and no call site: BR-26, BR-25, DRW-29,
'     SA 2026-10-17 ("add action to access history")
'
' Scope: this process is the whole life of a goal's progress measures — what is measured, and what
' it stood at. Framing the goal itself is BP05, judging it is BP07. The goals overview reads goals
' and not their measures, so this process reads its own at the entry; the goal it starts from is one
' the user already has in front of them.
'
' Call-site history: the measure lifecycle was drawn in BP05 until 2026-10-10 and moved here on the
' Software Architect's ruling, so that one process holds the measure and the other the commitment.
' BP05.06 to BP05.10 are retired there and are never reused.
'
' Call-site collapsing: a numeric check-in and a boolean check-in are two variations of one
' request. The type is the measure's, already fixed when the measure was added, so the payload
' differs and the operation does not. The inferred status belongs to the check-out (BP07), not
' here: a check-in records a data point and judges nothing.

pool "User" {
  start "A commitment to measure, or progress to record"
  :Work a progress measure;
  rule BR-118
  note "A goal's measures are its own sub-items and have no page of their own: they are already on the Goals view, read with the goals. This process acts on what is there."

  if "What needs doing?" then "add or change what counts"
    :Define a measure;
    rule BR-121
    :Submit the measure;
    send "Edit a progress measure" to editIn
    receive "The editing outcome" as measureSaved
    note "Numeric carries a start value, a target, a unit and a direction, and its current value starts at the start value; boolean carries done and not done, starting at not done. The type is editable like the start value, the target and the unit, and the recorded check-ins are left as they stand."
    end "Measure defined"

  elseif "What needs doing?" then "reorder them"
    :Order a measure;
    send "Reorder progress measures" to reorderIn
    receive "The ordering outcome" as reordered
    note "The check-in history hangs on the measure's identity, never on its position."
    end "Measures ordered"

  elseif "What needs doing?" then "set one aside"
    :Archive a measure;
    send "Archive a progress measure" to measureArchiveIn
    receive "The archiving outcome" as measureArchived
    note "A measure takes its own check-in history with it and brings it back with it. A project parented on it keeps its parent, which still exists."
    end "Measure set aside"

  elseif "What needs doing?" then "drop one"
    :Remove a measure;
    send "Remove a progress measure" to removeIn
    receive "The removal outcome" as removed
    note "Its check-in history goes with it, unasked, and nothing else does, so there is nothing to disclose and nothing to approve: a project parented on it survives minus the link."
    end "Measure removed"

  elseif "What needs doing?" then "record where one stands"
    :Check in on a measure;
    rule BR-121
    :Submit the check-in;
    send "Record a progress check-in" to checkInIn
    receive "The check-in outcome" as recorded
    note "Numeric takes the value the current value moves to. Boolean takes done and not done. A note is optional either way. Nothing is read first: the measure and where it stands arrived with the goals."
    end "Progress recorded"

  elseif "What needs doing?" then "look at the ones set aside"
    :Open the archived measures (BP15);
    note "An archived measure is listed under the goal it belongs to, in the Goals archive. Reading it, bringing it back and destroying it are their own process (BP15)."
    end "Archive opened"

  endif
}

system pool "Bearing" {
  messageStart "Check-in submitted" as checkInIn
  call "BP06.02_RecordProgressCheckIn" "Record a progress check-in" {
    :Append the check-in and move the measure's current value;
    rule BR-28
    :Report the outcome;
  }
  send "The check-in outcome" to recorded
  note "The history is append-only, so a date that already carries a check-in takes another and each is its own data point. The current value is what the latest one says, and the start value until there is one. A check-in records a data point and infers no status."
  end "Check-in answered"

  messageStart "Measure submitted" as editIn
  call "BP06.03_EditProgressMeasure" "Edit a progress measure" {
    :Store the edit;
    rule BR-28
    :Report the outcome;
  }
  send "The editing outcome" to measureSaved
  note "There is no untyped measure. The type is editable like the start value, the target and the unit, and the check-ins already recorded are left as they stand, each in the type it was recorded under."
  end "Measure answered"

  messageStart "Measure reordering requested" as reorderIn
  call "BP06.05_ReorderProgressMeasures" "Reorder progress measures" {
    :Apply the new order;
    :Report the outcome;
  }
  send "The ordering outcome" to reordered
  end "Measure reordering answered"

  messageStart "Measure archiving requested" as measureArchiveIn
  call "BP06.11_ArchiveProgressMeasure" "Archive a progress measure" {
    :Archive the measure;
    rule BR-23
    :Report the outcome;
  }
  send "The archiving outcome" to measureArchived
  note "Its check-in history goes with it and comes back with it, into a live goal. While it is away it is frozen, so nothing is recorded against it."
  end "Archiving answered"

  messageStart "Measure removal requested" as removeIn
  call "BP06.07_RemoveProgressMeasure" "Remove a progress measure" {
    :Remove the measure;
    rule BR-115
    :Report the outcome;
  }
  send "The removal outcome" to removed
  end "Removal answered"
}

@endbpmn
